Fundamentals of Vacuum Technology — Walter Umrath and contributors (@gas-leybold: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gas-sources) { r_1S93A5X32978GSHZH4CF96VPQR
Walter Umrath, reviser/compiler, with the named contributors. *Fundamentals of Vacuum Technology*, Leybold, edition 2016. [Official reading guide](https://www.leybold.com/en/knowledge/vacuum-fundamentals), [complete 200-page book](https://www.leybold.com/content/dam/brands/leybold/downloads/brochures/general-brochures/Fundamentals_of_Vacuum_Technology_EN.pdf).

Read chapter 1 gradually with the introductory Records, then the whole book through the pump, measurement, gas-analysis, leak-testing, maintenance and application sections. Reconstruct the quantitative examples independently and keep the units attached to empirical coefficients. Revisit complete sections when an actual system differs from the introductory model.

The official PDF, cover, preface and contents were inspected on 30 October 2026, with selected physical, conductance, displacement/gas-ballast, pump and backing-system discussions. The preface dates this edition to December 2016. Product names and performance examples are historical teaching examples; the publisher itself distinguishes explanatory data from guaranteed equipment properties.

Authorized free publisher reading; no blanket open adaptation licence was established. Preserve contributor and component credits, and keep the book external. The material is a broad technical spine, complemented by research papers and metrology sources where a handbook's simplified treatment needs deeper analysis.

